{"2077251628592181451":{"a":"<p>Echoes of My Father</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ef9NK-RaNZE\">YouTube</a></p>\n<div class=\"embed embed-youtube\"><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/Ef9NK-RaNZE?enablejsapi=1\" title=\"YouTube\" allowfullscreen referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\"></iframe><p class=\"embed-fallback\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ef9NK-RaNZE\">Watch on YouTube</a></p></div>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\" data-conversation=\"none\" data-dnt=\"true\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/2021101473199751379\">https://x.com/i/status/2021101473199751379</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 2077251628592181451</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/2077251628592181451\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2026-07-15T04:39:16Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>thread</dt><dd>2894</dd><dt>thread_count</dt><dd>3031</dd><dt>conversation</dt><dd>1972960487148298273</dd>\n</dl>"},"2077296342892753027":{"a":"<p>@CCGhostbusters The biggest misconception, and perhaps problem, with this device is that it is actually a time teleporter of sorts. It doesn&#x27;t move the spook in space. It just moves them forward 500 years in time.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/2077042796016386240\">https://x.com/i/status/2077042796016386240</a></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/CCGhostbusters/status/2077042796016386240\">https://x.com/CCGhostbusters/status/2077042796016386240</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 2077296342892753027</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/2077296342892753027\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2026-07-15T07:36:57Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"2077301821433893168":{"a":"<p>Well, it is demonic but you simply do not understand what a demon is. On your computer there is a service (aka Daemon) which watches the mouse move in your hand and mimics the movement on the screen. You can use a joystick instead of a mouse. Or tablet. Or eye tracker. <a href=\"https://x.com/AlchemyAmerican/status/2077095508472922566\">Tweet by @AlchemyAmerican</a></p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/AlchemyAmerican/status/2077095508472922566\">https://x.com/AlchemyAmerican/status/2077095508472922566</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 2077301821433893168</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/2077301821433893168\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2026-07-15T07:58:43Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"2077307405176623301":{"a":"<p>So many engineers totally miss the fact that a closed loop of copper or silver wire is equivalent to a permanent magnet when exposed to fluctuating fields. Lower conductance or inherently magnetic metals can leave one with the wrong impression. <a href=\"https://x.com/caleb_friesen/status/2076961331161301215\">Tweet by @caleb_friesen</a></p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/caleb_friesen/status/2076961331161301215\">https://x.com/caleb_friesen/status/2076961331161301215</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 2077307405176623301</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/2077307405176623301\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2026-07-15T08:20:54Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"2077308717276570103":{"a":"<p>So, detective stuff most people don&#x27;t notice. Appropriate for a detective show like ghostbusters. Deep in the background noise of some of these episode recordings you can hear morse code. What is that? VHS VCR head records frequencies used for airport non directional navigation.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/2077123084759269614\">https://x.com/i/status/2077123084759269614</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 2077308717276570103</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/2077308717276570103\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2026-07-15T08:26:07Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"2077308936194027775":{"a":"<p>See if you can tell which airport these VHS recordings were made near by listening to the morse code in the noise.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/2077308717276570103\">https://x.com/i/status/2077308717276570103</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 2077308936194027775</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/2077308936194027775\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2026-07-15T08:26:59Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"2077309380974801092":{"a":"<p>The spinning of the VHS record head would literally VOR encode the LF/MF non directional beacon phasing on the tape along with your TV program. Effectively allowing the tape to be triangulated if it picks up 2 or more NDBs.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/2077308717276570103\">https://x.com/i/status/2077308717276570103</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 2077309380974801092</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/2077309380974801092\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2026-07-15T08:28:45Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"2077311043064188979":{"a":"<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/760402660017123328\">Tweet by @DavidLNorris</a></p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/760402660017123328\">https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/760402660017123328</a></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/2077307405176623301\">https://x.com/i/status/2077307405176623301</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 2077311043064188979</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/2077311043064188979\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2026-07-15T08:35:21Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>zxx</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"2077312143062343793":{"a":"<p>3D printing motors is not as hard as one might think as well. If you can print directly in iron and copper then you are done. Thermoplastics turn out not to be a great idea around the bearings which get hot. The UV cure resin and copper wire work great.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1597099352027463681\">Tweet by @DavidLNorris</a></p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1597099352027463681\">https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1597099352027463681</a></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/2077307405176623301\">https://x.com/i/status/2077307405176623301</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 2077312143062343793</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/2077312143062343793\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2026-07-15T08:39:44Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"207